# Env

Copy to `.env` locally. After merge, Developer sets **secrets** on Railway (`TELNYX_API_KEY`, `XAI_API_KEY`, `API_KEY`, `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`). Do not place real PSTN calls from this repo. Tests mock Telnyx, xAI, and OpenAI. Never put API keys in code.

## Required for outbound calls

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `TELNYX_API_KEY` | Telnyx Call Control API (Bearer). Set on Railway after merge. |
| `XAI_API_KEY` | xAI Grok Voice Live 2. Set on Railway after merge. |
| `API_KEY` | Bearer token for `POST /api/outbound` and `GET /api/calls/:id`. Set on Railway after merge. |
| `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | Public HTTPS origin. Telnyx webhook = `{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/webhooks/telnyx`. |

## Telnyx (non-secret, TRNSF/Nuno)

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `TELNYX_CONNECTION_ID` | `3041732714274227469` | Call Control app **TRNSX-Outbound-Grok**. |
| `TELNYX_OUTBOUND_VOICE_PROFILE_ID` | `3041732644774610184` | Outbound Voice Profile bound to that app (not sent on each dial). |
| `FROM_NUMBER` | `+351210210260` | Caller ID. |

## Voice / model

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GROK_VOICE` | `ara` | Default Grok Voice Live 2 voice when `POST /api/outbound` omits `grok_voice`. Per-call override: `grok_voice` (`ara` \| `eve` \| `rex` \| `sal` \| `leo`). Male pt-PT: `rex` (confident) / `leo` (authoritative). `GET /health` reports this env default. |
| `GROK_MODEL` | `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0` | Grok Voice Live 2 model. |
| `GROK_VOICE_SPEED` | `1.05` | Documented xAI `audio.output.speed` (0.7–1.5). Slight liveliness nudge above the API default `1.0`. **Do not change.** Pre-audio delay is cut with `session.reasoning.effort: none` in code (xAI default is `high`) — not by raising speed. |

## ElevenLabs (LIVE — hybrid)

Grok Voice Live stays on the call for input audio / transcripts / text / `end_call`. When `tts_provider=elevenlabs` and `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` is set, Telnyx hears Benedita, not Grok `ara`. Developer sets `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` on Railway after merge (secret — never in git).

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | _(empty)_ | Secret. Required before `tts_provider=elevenlabs` is accepted (`ready.elevenlabs` + `audioPathActive`). |
| `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID` | `NkpT2jezTenCDRKHkWiX` | Benedita - PT-PT (Alfa teste). **20-char id, letters `Ten` — not `Tn`, not `Ln`.** `NkpT2jezTnCDRKHkWiX` is `voice_not_found` (mute). Nuno A/B: set this to Joana `nJ5NFqyKb8kn9JBPmo6i` to swap the live voice. |
| `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_ALT` | `nJ5NFqyKb8kn9JBPmo6i` | Documented A/B candidate (Joana — Natural and gentle, warm European Portuguese conversational feminine). Does **not** play unless copied into `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID`. Exposed on `GET /health` as `tts.elevenlabs.voiceIdAlt` / `recommendedVoiceAlt`. |
| `ELEVENLABS_MODEL` | `eleven_v3` | Default. Quality over TTFB. Optional `eleven_v3_conversational` (~280ms later turns, same audio tags). `eleven_flash_v2_5` is a quality tradeoff and must not receive audio tags. |
| `ELEVENLABS_OPTIMIZE_STREAMING_LATENCY` | `3` | Sent **only** for models that support it (flash / turbo / multilingual_v2). **Omitted for `eleven_v3` and `eleven_v3_conversational`** — those models return HTTP 400 `unsupported_model` if the query param is present, which used to empty the greeting cache (`cache_frames=0`) and mute the callee on unlock. |
| `ELEVENLABS_VAD_SILENCE_MS` | `130` | Optional extra `server_vad` silence when `tts_provider=elevenlabs`. Shared default is already 130 (`GROK_VAD_SILENCE_MS`). |

If `POST /api/outbound` sends `tts_provider: "elevenlabs"` without `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, the API returns **503 `elevenlabs_not_configured`**. When the key is set, `GET /health` shows `tts.elevenlabs.audioPathActive: true` and TRNSF can pass `tts_provider=elevenlabs` to play Benedita on the PSTN leg.

## OpenAI Realtime (LIVE — speech-to-speech)

When `tts_provider=openai`, OpenAI Realtime owns **STT + dialogue + voice** (not chained TTS). Telnyx still owns the PSTN leg. Grok is not used on that call. Fail closed: missing `OPENAI_API_KEY` → **503 `openai_not_configured`**; Realtime WebSocket not ready before dial → **503 `openai_session_failed`**. Never falls back to Grok ara.

The Realtime WebSocket is **pre-connected at dial** and the first greeting is generated while muted (generate early / speak late). After `waitForCallee` unlock, cached PCMU is flushed to Telnyx.

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | _(empty)_ | Secret. Required before `tts_provider=openai` is accepted (`ready.openai` + `audioPathActive`). |
| `OPENAI_REALTIME_MODEL` | `gpt-realtime-2.1` | OpenAI Realtime speech-to-speech model. |
| `OPENAI_VOICE` | `coral` | Feminine expressive Realtime voice for PT. OpenAI also recommends `marin` for quality. **Voice is immutable after first audio** (the pre-cached greeting). |
| `OPENAI_BASE` | `https://api.openai.com` | HTTPS origin; converted to `wss://…/v1/realtime`. |

Optional request field `openai_voice` overrides `OPENAI_VOICE` for that call (`alloy` \| `ash` \| `ballad` \| `coral` \| `echo` \| `sage` \| `shimmer` \| `verse` \| `marin` \| `cedar`).

## GPT-Live-1 / ChatGPT Voice (`tts_provider=gpt-live`)

Same `OPENAI_API_KEY` as Realtime. Connects to `wss://api.openai.com/v1/live/sessions` (not `/v1/realtime`). Default language lock is **European Portuguese** (`pt-PT`): live instructions are written in pt-PT; default voice is `marin` (multilingual quality). Do **not** default to `bossa` or `tempo` — those are Brazilian Portuguese voices.

Aliases accepted on `tts_provider`: `gpt-live` \| `gpt-live-1` \| `chatgpt-live` \| `chatgpt-live-1` (stored as `gpt-live`).

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `OPENAI_LIVE_MODEL` | `gpt-live-1` | GPT-Live speech-to-speech model. |
| `OPENAI_LIVE_VOICE` | `marin` | Default GPT-Live voice. Override per call with `gpt_live_voice` or `openai_voice`. |
| `OPENAI_LIVE_DELEGATE_MODEL` | `gpt-5.6-terra` | Responses backend for `end_call` / `send_dtmf`. |

Missing `OPENAI_API_KEY` → **503 `openai_not_configured`**. Live WebSocket not ready → **503 `gpt_live_session_failed`**. Never falls back to Grok ara.

Optional request field `grok_voice` overrides `GROK_VOICE` for `tts_provider=grok` (`ara` \| `eve` \| `rex` \| `sal` \| `leo`). Optional `ivr: true` adds IVR keypress guidance so the agent uses the `send_dtmf` tool instead of speaking numbers.

Language on each call: `pt-PT` | `en-GB` | `en-US` (default `pt-PT` if omitted).

Persona (`persona` or `greeting`) and `objective` come from `POST /api/outbound`. There is no branded spoken default and no recording notice. If both `persona` and `greeting` are omitted, the service composes Lisbon time-of-day + **caller identity** («sou a secretária» / “this is the secretary”) + a short natural ask derived from `objective` (never `Olá`/`Hello`, never a ROLEPLAY/prompt dump, never «bem-vindo ao restaurante»). Optional `spokenAsk` is a clean one-line ask. Optional `timezone` (IANA, default `Europe/Lisbon`) selects the local clock. `waitForCallee` does not require `greeting`.

On `tts_provider=elevenlabs` with `eleven_v3` / `eleven_v3_conversational`, the HTTP TTS body is tagged `[warmly]` / `[curious]` / `[sighs]` (performance only — stripped from transcripts and never sent to Grok `force_message`).

## Turn-taking (Grok server_vad)

Phone-tuned so the agent answers promptly after the callee stops (shared default **130ms** silence for Grok, ElevenLabs, and OpenAI). The Telnyx↔Grok / OpenAI bridge forwards audio immediately (no extra debounce after `speech_stopped`). Override if needed:

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GROK_VAD_THRESHOLD` | `0.5` | VAD activation (`0.1`–`0.9`). |
| `GROK_VAD_SILENCE_MS` | `130` | End-of-turn silence in ms before the model replies. Shared across providers. Raise toward 160 if barge-in chopping shows up. |
| `GROK_VAD_PREFIX_PADDING_MS` | `200` | Audio kept before detected speech start (barge-in). |
| `GROK_VAD_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` | `12000` | Idle timeout (not the turn gap). |
| `GROK_CALLEE_SPEECH_GRACE_MS` | `350` | After answer/stream start, ignore `speech_started` (ringback/noise). Speech that starts during grace and is still going (or already stopped at word length) unlocks as soon as this window ends. Transcripts («estou») unlock immediately even during grace. |
| `GROK_CALLEE_MIN_SPEECH_MS` | `80` | Floor for treating an in-grace burst as real speech (pending unlock at grace end). After grace, first `speech_started` unlocks immediately — no `awaiting_min_duration` stall. Short greeting transcripts still unlock immediately. |
| `GROK_HANGUP_PLAYOUT_MS` | `1000` | Extra Telnyx playout after Grok `response.done` before hangup on `end_call`. |

## Optional

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `RESULT_WEBHOOK` | `POST` JSON when a call ends. Empty disables. |
| `TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY` | Account Ed25519 public key. When set, `/webhooks/telnyx` verifies signatures. |
| `XAI_BASE_URL` | Default `https://api.x.ai`. |
| `TELNYX_API_BASE` | Default `https://api.telnyx.com`. |
| `PORT` | Railway injects this. Default `3000`. |
| `MAX_CALL_SECONDS` | Hard cap before hangup. Default `600`. |

This service is **outbound-only** and is **not** Alice.
